{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00349",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.56,
      "end_seconds": 4.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Good morning, you know, doctor. Can I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.18,
      "end_seconds": 10.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Right, of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.02,
      "end_seconds": 24.37,
      "duration_seconds": 12.35,
      "text": "Oh, you know, I wanted to get pain low in the pelvis looked at. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.78,
      "end_seconds": 27.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.3,
      "end_seconds": 40.92,
      "duration_seconds": 11.62,
      "text": "Ever since... since last night, really. I just want to get back to normal, really. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.24,
      "end_seconds": 44.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "What's the pattern, is it there all day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.69,
      "end_seconds": 47.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "It's on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.38,
      "end_seconds": 50.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.57,
      "end_seconds": 59.84,
      "duration_seconds": 8.27,
      "text": "Pain during sex goes along with it, most of the time. The pain during sex? That's been for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.15,
      "end_seconds": 63.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Right. Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.13,
      "end_seconds": 80.78,
      "duration_seconds": 16.65,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.71,
      "end_seconds": 83.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Any fever or vomiting at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.01,
      "end_seconds": 89.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "No fever or vomiting, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.47,
      "end_seconds": 93.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Any vaginal discharge, bleeding between periods or missed period at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.51,
      "end_seconds": 100.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "No vaginal discharge, bleeding between periods or missed period, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.07,
      "end_seconds": 105.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.03,
      "end_seconds": 107.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.35,
      "end_seconds": 112.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.79,
      "end_seconds": 115.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.62,
      "end_seconds": 119.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.76,
      "end_seconds": 126.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "It's iron tablets, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.01,
      "end_seconds": 130.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.38,
      "end_seconds": 135.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Two months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.33,
      "end_seconds": 138.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.36,
      "end_seconds": 142.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.48,
      "end_seconds": 147.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.7,
      "end_seconds": 151.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Yeah, yes, ibuprofen, it gives me stomach pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.16,
      "end_seconds": 169.3,
      "duration_seconds": 16.14,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.74,
      "end_seconds": 173.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "I, I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.36,
      "end_seconds": 175.1,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.66,
      "end_seconds": 176.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "I've never smoked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.45,
      "end_seconds": 180.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.63,
      "end_seconds": 188.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "Busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.75,
      "end_seconds": 196.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.05,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.89,
      "end_seconds": 205.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "I've had eczema, yes. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.79,
      "end_seconds": 209.56,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.74,
      "end_seconds": 218.87,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "Right, uh, I have low haemoglobin, for about ten years. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.39,
      "end_seconds": 227.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "Okay, low haemoglobin, that's already on your record. Good to know. Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.36,
      "end_seconds": 238.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.8,
      "end_seconds": 259.95,
      "duration_seconds": 12.15,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 80 beats a minute, temperature is 36.4 degrees, respiratory rate 16. And SpO2 99 percent on room air, pressure 108 over 74. Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.03,
      "end_seconds": 274.16,
      "duration_seconds": 13.13,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.52,
      "end_seconds": 279.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.84,
      "end_seconds": 282.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Look straight ahead for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.27,
      "end_seconds": 300.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "There's tenderness in the lower tummy on the left, and no guarding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.67,
      "end_seconds": 302.37,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.77,
      "end_seconds": 331.93,
      "duration_seconds": 26.16,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.28,
      "end_seconds": 336.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Well, you know, okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.59,
      "end_seconds": 349.43,
      "duration_seconds": 11.84,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is chronic pelvic pain, possibly endometriosis. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out a pelvic infection yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.94,
      "end_seconds": 353.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.75,
      "end_seconds": 372.43,
      "duration_seconds": 17.68,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's chronic pelvic pain, possibly endometriosis, and we'll know more once the a pelvic ultrasound is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had pain low in the pelvis, since last night, and no vaginal discharge or bleeding between periods."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.72,
      "end_seconds": 375.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.94,
      "end_seconds": 381.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Okay, is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.7,
      "end_seconds": 385.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Oh, I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 386.67,
      "end_seconds": 409.84,
      "duration_seconds": 23.17,
      "text": "We should do a pelvic ultrasound for pelvic pain. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. A heat pad and some gentle movement help many people, and a pain diary helps me see a pattern. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. I'll also refer you to a gynaecologist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 410.64,
      "end_seconds": 413.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "So, sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 413.79,
      "end_seconds": 422.56,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the pain becomes sudden and severe or you faint, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.1,
      "end_seconds": 425.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 426.86,
      "end_seconds": 435.88,
      "duration_seconds": 9.02,
      "text": "Let's review you in four weeks. So, before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 437.15,
      "end_seconds": 442.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "So, uh, I come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 444.26,
      "end_seconds": 448.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, I think we're finished. Is everything clear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 449.32,
      "end_seconds": 455.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "Well, um, I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    }
  ]
}